// The hardware-handshake operation model, one instance per handshake-capable
// channel (docs/wb_dma_operation_model.md §4, `dma_hs_c`).
//
// The participant here is the PERIPHERAL DEVICE, not the processor: this is
// the model a device-side consumer -- or a requesting IP's own operation model
// -- composes with. All three operations were already blocking in the first
// pass; a sideband has no state to poll, so its operations arrive at the right
// shape naturally.
//
// No base address, and that absence is the point: this interface has no
// address space at all, which is what distinguishes a sideband from a bus
// interface.
//
// None of these three is ever a driver state. request_chunk() waits on a pin
// with no processor involved; dma_nd_i and dma_rest_i have no register bit
// anywhere in §4, so software cannot invoke them at all.

import wb_dma_hs_pkg::*;

component wb_dma_hs_c {

    // Index into dma_req_i / dma_ack_o / dma_nd_i / dma_rest_i.
    int     chan;

    // §3.9 requires dma_nd_i to lead dma_req_i by at least two cycles.
    int     nd_lead_cycles = 2;
}
